#HTML^<p>The Wild Bunch is mostly Sinclair BASIC. The commercial tape stores the
program as a single <code>PROGRAM</code> block with a one-line stub that
<code>LIST</code> will show, then the real tokenised program with line 15's
header deliberately corrupted so listing stops. This page is a recovered
<code>LIST</code> of that program (507 lines). Line 15 is
reconstructed from the prompt text and the pre-production tape; every other
line is taken from the post-load snapshot.</p>
<p>Line 1 enters the machine-code stub with
<code>RANDOMIZE USR (VARS-116)</code>. The digits in the line say
<code>140</code>, but the hidden floating-point value is <code>116</code>.
In this snapshot that is #R$E933. The tap2sna start address
#R$E973 sits further into the same stub. Game logic, text and data are
the BASIC below; the stub holds graphics helpers and the USR entry.</p>
<pre class="basic" style="white-space:pre; overflow:auto; font-size:12px; line-height:1.35">
   1 RANDOMIZE USR ((PEEK 23627)+((PEEK 23628)*256)-116)
  15 PRINT &amp;quot;WHAT NAME DO YOU GO BY?&amp;quot;: INPUT &amp;quot;ENTER NAME &amp;quot;; LINE N$: IF N$=&amp;quot;&amp;quot; THEN GO TO VAL &amp;quot;15&amp;quot;
  20 BEEP .4,-10: CLS : PRINT AT 8,3;&amp;quot;ENTER LEVEL OF DIFFICULTY&amp;quot;: INPUT &amp;quot; LEVEL 1,2 OR 3 &amp;quot;; LINE E$: LET E$=E$+&amp;quot; &amp;quot;: IF CODE E$(1)&amp;gt;51 OR CODE E$(1)&amp;lt;49 THEN GO TO VAL &amp;quot;20&amp;quot;
  22 LET LV=VAL E$+U
  30 BEEP .5,30: CLS : PRINT AT 10,10;&amp;quot;PLEASE WAIT&amp;quot;: LET LM=3: LET SC=O: LET JB=O: LET L=6: LET CS=1500: LET DT=O: RANDOMIZE O: DIM T(5,5): RESTORE 9110: FOR N=U TO 5: FOR A=U TO 5: READ S: LET T(N,A)=S: NEXT A: NEXT N
  40 LET CS=1450: DIM U(5,INT PI): RESTORE VAL &amp;quot;9120&amp;quot;: FOR N=U TO 5: FOR A=U TO 3: READ S: LET U(N,A)=S: NEXT A: NEXT N
  50 DIM K$(16,20): RESTORE VAL &amp;quot;9140&amp;quot;: FOR N=U TO 16: READ K$(N): NEXT N
  60 DIM K(16): RESTORE VAL &amp;quot;9145&amp;quot;: FOR N=U TO 16: READ K(N): NEXT N:
  70 DIM I(16): FOR N=U TO 16: LET I(N)=O: NEXT N: LET I(6)=5: LET I(4)=U: DIM R(5): RESTORE VAL &amp;quot;9095&amp;quot;: FOR N=U TO 5: READ R(N): NEXT N: DIM D$(5,19)
 115 FOR N=U TO 5: RESTORE VAL &amp;quot;9000&amp;quot;+INT (RND*12)+U: READ l$: LET D$(n)=L$
